This is the log that I kept of my Pri-Mal-Elf-Cha game from a month
ago. I found the time to clean it up, and present it to the NetHack
community:

Yogi the Elven Priest, 11/12/06

12:30 PM
I reached Minetown with my Elven priest without much difficulty. I
entered one of the two hardware shops and opened a chest.
It contained a wand that cost 666 zorkmids. Evidently, it was a
base-500 wand with the +33% attached.
It was either death or wishing, and either one would be great for my
purposes.
With the wand of death, I could kill the shopkeeper, the guards, and
the Lawful priest.
With a wand of wishing, I was guaranteed at least 4 wands of death.
What was there to lose? So I zapped it.
"Ahem. Usage fee. 166 zorkmids. What would you like to wish for?"
I soon recieved 2 blessed scrolls of charging, a blessed +2 gray dragon
scale mail, and the blessed greased fixed Master Key of Thievery.
Recharge. Blessed fixed greased wand of death. Lock the door, and zap
the shopkeeper. No angry guard.
Next move: Dig away one wall of the temple, for easy shooting from
outside. But first, kill that annoying nymph with the wand.
Bye-bye, priest. Converted the altar to Chaotic on the third try.
Better scram before my luck starts changing for the worse.

1:30 PM
A blessed spellbook of identify, and we're off.
Sokoban went quite well. I made a mistake on the first level, but it's
the one that's forgiving. I was careful for the rest.
Managed to kill a gray unicorn, and fixed the poison damage that I took
from a spellbook. Slew the zoo, and got a bag of holding.

2:00 PM
Went down further, found the last incarnation of myself that I just
played. A cursed magic lamp, but it was cursed in the last game, too.
Keep descending, make some holy water, bless the bag of holding.
Identify more items. Routine.

2:30 PM
Find a Neutral altar on level 8. There's 53 coins on an adjacent
square, and a full icebox on another.
Can't believe my luck. Open the icebox, and take out the elf corpse
that someone left. One sacrifice, and we're good.
Sacrifice the rest, and get Orcrist. Unrestricted broadsword lets me
use Stormbringer if I get it later on.
Go down two levels, and kill a floating eye. I get intrinsic telepathy
and an amulet of reflection. Oh, the irony.
Lunch break.

3:00 PM
Descending as usual. A leprechaun hall, a beehive, and a throne room.
Waste of turns hunting everything down. Taking a break.

7:00 PM
Back at it; went down another level. A zoo.
Another zoo and Medusa's later, and I'm at the castle.
There were only a few liches and golden nagas, so I didn't bother to
use the drawbridge.
A wand of wishing (0:3). What could I wish for? I never thought I'd be
in this situation.
The death beam whizzes past me. I'll identify the soldier's wand when I
get 15 mana.
The throne vanished immediately. I'll try the chest.
An electric shock, no less. The wand of death goes up in smoke. I'm
down to 20-odd health. That was close.
There are three pairs of combat boots in the armoury, but I don't have
levitation or jumping.
Maybe Perseus does?

8:00 PM
Back a level, and I show Medusa her reflection. I rarely pack a looking
glass with me; looks like it was useful this time.
Nope. Perseus has a shield, scimitar, and sack, but no boots.
With no way to cross the water, I'll have to use a cursed scroll of
teleportation.
Good thing I have the Master Key of Thievery.
The cursed dark green potion I picked up happens to be levitation. I'll
save it for the swamp.

8:30 PM
In the Valley, I'm jolted by a chest again, and lose my ring of free
action.
Shock resistance is needed, desperately.
Deja vu is really striking my priests.
This is the third one I'm playing today: the first two were both killed
by winter wolf cubs.

9:00 PM
With the blessed potion of levitation, I entered the armoury.
Large creatures are still hitting quite hard on me; I need to improve
my AC.
I have 9 wishes left. Perhaps they'll all go to magic markers?
I float gently to the floor. The combat boots are speed boots. It's
good to have some to spare.

9:30 PM
Reached level 14 through combat.
Going to get Stormbringer; trying to sacrifice.
A few cursed scrolls later, I have Yeenoghu and Juiblex in Sokoban.
Trollsbane, too. Oh wow.
But Frost Brand is quite decent, and is better against demons than
Stormbringer.

10:00 PM
Going to the quest; clearing the last few human zombies.
Trying to lure the wraiths, to little avail. Nor can those vampires be
slain in a single hit; hello carpal tunnel.

10:30 PM
The quest-locate level. The DevTeam wasn't kidding about "a large
graveyard".
Teleport control is my saviour. Can't kill me if you can't catch me,
can you?
Bash a few zombies in the doorway, and downstairs it is.
Hmm. This looks like the Monk's quest. A couple of death rays, and the
Mitre is mine.

11:00 PM
I toss the Bell to the Arch Priest to see if he would catch it. He
doesn't, and it lands at his feet.
He's not going anywhere, so I help him out. He doesn't seem too pleased
that he's been teleported.
I grab the Bell and scram. The quest guardians are beating up on me,
and I sidle up to him to try to calm him down.
Bad move. I'm expelled from the quest. Good thing I've got the Bell on
me.

11:30 PM
Time to return to Gehennom. Dump some items to accomodate the Bell, and
we're off.
But first, enchant the Mitre. +5? Not a problem.
Much tedium. Magic mapping helps a lot; keeps me sane.
Hello Asemodeus, have two bits and be off.
Baalzebub brings trouble; I finish him off anyway.
Vlad? He crumbles to dust in a few short strokes.
Attach the candles to the Candelabrum, and leave.
I'll have a special treat for Orcus, when I come back up.

12:00 AM
Run away! Run away!
No need to flee from these puny creatures; a rubber chicken clears the
way.
Another wand of death? Gratis, from our favorite resident of the only
town in Hell.
Frost Brand passes harmlessly through the shades, but not magic
missiles.

12:30 AM
Tagged the vibrating square. Time to pay the purple @ a visit.
Rodney dodges a few death rays but eventually goes down. I dust off the
Book of the Dead and head down again.
The dungeon walls crumble around me! I'm at the top of a staircase
leading down.

1:00 AM
No sleep tonight, I'm afraid. The Amulet is just within reach.
Someone summons Geryon; I hear some noises in the distance.
The good & shows up near me; I burn Elbereth and fend him off.
The Amulet? Yes. The Wizard was never able to fetch it for me when he
shows up.
Looks like it takes a lawful demon to do the job. I'm out of here; no
need to touch the Sanctum.

1:30 AM
The mysterious force doesn't bother me much.
Rodney shows up infrequently; I blast him when he does.
Up, up, up; controlled teleport when I can, wand of digging when I
can't.
The Valley? I pat myself on my back.
Just a few more levels to go.

2:00 AM
Beware, mortal, for there shall be no return! Still climb? Yes.
Well done, and I'm ready to face the final test. Rodney bites the dust,
and so does the minotaur.
The Elvenking has no quarrel with me, and I leave him alone.
I attempt cast a forgotten spell, then read a scroll of gold detection.
I burn my wands of digging, and the rest become useless. Welcome to the
Plane of Air.
Time to gain control over my movements. One charge left in my wand of
teleportation; I have to dodge these elementals.
I'm ambushed and surrounded by nasties. Should I try to fight it out?
The minotaur is caught in the magical explosion! A well-used last
charge.
They've been scattered, and I make a beeline for the detected portal.

2:30 AM
A quick trap detection, and I'm in the portal almost immediately. No
worries.
The Plane of Water. I take off my ring of levitation. I feel heavier?
Bad move.
I pull myself out and search around for the portal. Finally, there it
is.
Anshar applauds my efforts. It's not over yet. I head for the middle
altar.
Death presents himself before me, and I cut him down. I bash a few
unfriendlies, and I check the altar.

3:00 AM
Cross-aligned. I make my way back. Which way now? Famine guards the
left, Pestilence holds the right.
I send a death beam in Famine's direction, and make my way up to the
altar.
Co-aligned. I check to make sure the Amulet is in my inventory, and I
offer it to Anshar...

Yogi, chaotic male elven Priest




